      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ERIN JO (2) brings the strongest exposed quality, with her last campaign including a ninth in the G2 The Roses at Doomben and a Listed Gold Coast Bracelet run behind Nightline. She resumes off two trials, has placed at both attempts around 1200m and reunites with Chad Schofield. Her stakes profile gives her a clear edge from the right gate. FROSTISEN (6) is the main danger fourth up after charging home at Kembla Grange last start despite covering ground and being steadied shortly after the start. Can race closer from the draw and take stopping. MOSCOW MAID (5) has been honest in stronger BM68 and FM BM72 races, with Tyler Schiller back aboard and first-time blinkers/visor adding interest. Should get the trip and place preferred. ROYAL SILVER (3) resumes from a longer break, but her 1200m record and two trials keep her in the mix after her Kembla Grange win last March. Respect.",
